@startuml
title LLM Gateway - internal structure (the harness around the model call)
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #B52330
  BackgroundColor #E8ECF4
  FontColor #202025
}
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FAF5F5
skinparam LegendBorderColor #B52330
top to bottom direction

component "Assistant Service" as AS #FFF4F4
component "Operator Console" as OC #FFF4F4
component "Policy Engine" as POL
component "LLM Provider (external, large)" as LLM #FFFFFF
component "Local Model Runtime (small)" as LMR #E8ECF4
component "Event Bus" as EB #E8ECF4

component "LLM Gateway" as GW {
  component "Input Guardrail" as IG
  component "Model Router" as RT
  component "Cache & Memory" as CM
  component "Output Guardrail" as OG
  component "Trace Log" as TR
}

IG -0)- AS : ILlmGateway (entry)
RT -0)- IG : IRoute
CM -0)- RT : ICacheMemory
OG -0)- RT : ICheckAnswer
TR -0)- RT : ILogExchange
POL -0)- RT : IOperatingMode
LLM -0)- RT : ILlmProvider
LMR -0)- RT : ILlmProvider
EB -0)- RT : IEventBus
TR -0)- OC : IReviewQueue

legend bottom
  The gateway is exposed to the Assistant Service as ILlmGateway; its first stage is the Input Guardrail.
  Only the Model Router calls the model provider, the cache, the output guardrail and the trace log.
  The router chooses the route from a value score and a cost estimate, using the mode and signals of IOperatingMode.
  Cache & Memory and Trace Log persist through IDataAccess (see the interface table).
endlegend
@enduml
